Declare rules_python's generated hub repos reproducible so they can use the repo contents
cache.

Upstream marked the downloading rules (`python_repository`, `uv_repository`) reproducible but
stopped short of the repos generated from them, which only write BUILD/bzl files derived
from their own attributes: `rules_python_internal`, `pythons_hub` and `uv`. Still true on
rules_python 2.x, so there is no version to bump to.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/python/private/internal_config_repo.bzl b/python/private/internal_config_repo.bzl
index 9fc301c..2576552 100644
--- a/python/private/internal_config_repo.bzl
+++ b/python/private/internal_config_repo.bzl
@@ -150,7 +150,11 @@ def _internal_config_repo_impl(rctx):
         _TRANSITION_SETTINGS_DEBUG_TEMPLATE.format(lines = "\n".join(debug_lines)),
     )
 
-    return None
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
 
 internal_config_repo = repository_rule(
     implementation = _internal_config_repo_impl,
